<title>URUGUAY: Uruguay to offer $100 mln in Eurobonds.</title>
<headline>Uruguay to offer $100 mln in Eurobonds.</headline>
<dateline>MONTEVIDEO 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uruguay plans to offer $100 million in 10-year Eurobonds priced at less than 182 basis points over U.S. Treasuries, according to Central Bank sources.</p>
<p>The bonds will be underwritten by Credit Suisse First Boston.</p>
<p>Uruguay's Economy Minister Luis Mosca will make a New York presentation Thursday on the issue, promoting recent advances in the Uruguayan economy such as low inflation and anticipated reductions in government spending, the sources said.</p>
<p>-- Esteban Israel, Montevideo Newsroom, 5982 92 03 36</p>
</text>
